+R2 is resolved. The matrix and implementation cohort now identify `reader-state.js:serializeLegacy()` or an equivalent shared lexical facade, all four production call sites, the bidirectional mapping, and CLI normalization before `_calendars.partition()` directory filtering. They explicitly preserve internal v1 edition/event/source identities, semantic location, forms, opaque choice IDs and unknown envelope values. Required old/new round-trip, canonical Share and Compare tests are stated. This is lexical compatibility around the same selected objects; a narrowed semantic identity still requires an explicit reader-state version migration.
